<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Resource-shrinker keep list. Partner-app has the same file with its own globs.

  `isShrinkResources = true` on the release build type removes any resource the shrinker cannot
  see referenced from code. Two string families are only ever resolved REFLECTIVELY, by a name
  built at runtime, so nothing statically references them and both are shrink candidates:

    error_*         ApiErrorParser.kt:118 — "error_" + the server error key, dots to underscores,
                    lowercased.
    loyalty_perks_* RewardsTab.kt:515 — the perk labelKey the API returns ("loyalty.perks.*"),
                    dots to underscores. resolveLabelKey has no prefix guard, so a labelKey the
                    backend sends outside that namespace would fall outside this glob and render
                    as the raw key; the 7 declared names cover every seeded labelKey today.

  The failure mode this file prevents is silent and reaches only the user: every backend error
  collapses to the generic fallback, and reward perks render "loyalty.perks.welcome_badge"
  instead of their label. Nothing fails to build, no test goes red. AGP's shrinker has
  string-prefix heuristics that may cover some of this, but "may" is not a contract.

  Adding a new reflectively-resolved string family means adding its glob here.
-->
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:keep="@string/error_*,@string/loyalty_perks_*" />
